id: storm-weather
name: Storm Weather
kind: battlefield
weather: true
rolls: true
profile: elemental-lightning
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The lightning. A 1(WT)-in-10 strike each Combat Round for 6(WT) Life Points, halved
  Awareness past Natural, and Impediment on a strike at Cataclysmic.
text: >
  Storm Weather: A flash of lightning illuminates the sky as a crash of thunder shatters
  the skies overhead, randomly striking down anyone willing to brave the storm.

  Connected Profile: Elemental (Lightning)

  Natural Weather (Tier 1) Effect(s):
  * At the start of each Combat Round, roll a 1d10. If the result is a 1(WT) or lower,
  you are struck by Lightning. Reduce your Life Points by 6(WT).

  Unnatural Weather (Tier 2) Effect(s):
  * Halve your Awareness.

  Cataclysmic Weather (Tier 3) Effect(s):
  * If you are struck by Lightning, you suffer from the Impediment Combat Condition until
  the end of the Combat Round.

---

# The first Battle Weather that cannot be written here whole, and the reason is worth
# saying plainly rather than leaving somebody to find the missing block.
#
# --- Natural (1), and Cataclysmic (3): the strike ---------------------------------------------------
#
# "Roll a 1d10. If the result is a 1(WT) or lower, you are struck by Lightning."
#
# A script in this language writes values. It cannot roll a die, hold the result and take
# one branch or the other on it - and it should not be able to: a script runs again every
# time the character is prepared, so a roll inside one would come out differently each time
# the sheet was opened, and the strike would land and unland as somebody scrolled.
#
# So the strike is an event rather than an effect. It lives in `strikeLightning` in
# combat.mjs - rolled once, shown on a card, and applied.
#
# Offered rather than fired. The start-of-round card carries an "Apply Battle Weather"
# button for anybody standing in a Weather whose file says `rolls: true`, and the player
# presses it. It was automatic first, and a number that arrives without anybody touching it
# is one nobody feels they had any part in - which matters more for a storm that may kill
# you than for almost anything else here.
#
# Once a Round. The card keeps the list of who has rolled, so a player who was away when it
# was posted still finds their button waiting.
#
# The Tier does three things at once there, which is what makes the card worth reading:
#
#   how likely  "a 1(WT) or lower" - one face in ten at Natural, three at Cataclysmic
#   how hard    6(WT) Life Points, so 6(bT) at Natural and 18(bT) at Cataclysmic
#   what it leaves  Impediment, at Cataclysmic and only on a strike
#
# "Until the end of the Combat Round" is a duration the turn edges could not express: it
# ends at the same moment for everybody, whoever is standing where in the Initiative Order.
# That is what `EDGES.ROUND` is, added for this and counted when the Round turns over.
#
# --- Unnatural (2): the Awareness -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Halve your Awareness."
#
# This half is an effect and stays here. Awareness feeds the Strike Roll, so the storm is
# the same trade Tornado Weather makes - it blinds you before it slows you.
#
# --- What is not built ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Connected Profile: Elemental (Lightning)." The Elemental Profiles are the Magic Profiles,
# and there are none in this system yet. Carried in the header and read by nobody.

[passive]
if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 2) {
  awareness *= 0.5;
}
